Repair the complete CommonJS source below. It should export `{ ReplyTracker }`. `begin(id)` accepts a non-empty string, rejects an already-pending ID with `RangeError`, records it, and returns the ID. `resolve(message)` accepts a plain object with exactly non-empty string `id` and own `payload`; it removes and returns `{ id, payload }` only when that ID is pending, otherwise returns `null`. Replies may arrive in any order. Returned objects must be fresh, but payload identity is intentionally preserved. `pending()` returns pending IDs in begin order. Malformed inputs throw `TypeError` without mutation, and empty state is valid. Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
class ReplyTracker {
  #pending = [];

  begin(id) {
    ReplyTracker.#id(id);
    if (this.#pending.includes(id)) throw new RangeError('id already pending');
    this.#pending.push(id);
    return id;
  }

  resolve(message) {
    ReplyTracker.#message(message);
    if (this.#pending.length === 0) return null;
    const id = this.#pending.shift();
    return { id, payload: message.payload };
  }

  pending() {
    return [...this.#pending];
  }

  static #id(id) {
    if (typeof id !== 'string' || id.length === 0) throw new TypeError('id must be non-empty');
  }

  static #message(message) {
    if (!message || typeof message !== 'object' || Array.isArray(message) || Object.getPrototypeOf(message) !== Object.prototype) throw new TypeError('message must be plain');
    const keys = Object.keys(message).sort();
    if (keys.length !== 2 || keys[0] !== 'id' || keys[1] !== 'payload') throw new TypeError('invalid message fields');
    this.#id(message.id);
  }
}

module.exports = { ReplyTracker };
```

